MID_LGV_3_M05_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kai_m01_001: It's been a long, difficult fight. But there have been\nbright moments too.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kai_m01_002: I made friends with lots of people. I was taught loads\nof things that I never imagined.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kai_m01_003: You were one of those teachers, Promised One.\nYour companionship can't ever be replaced.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Kai_m01: <BLN>I made friends with lots of people...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Bel_m01_001: After Mars told us to rescue Saramis, he took a step\nback from our affairs.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Bel_m01_002: Fair enough. Gods may not be seen to interfere.\nHe wants to hand the world to us humans.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Bel_m01_003: As the inheritor of the Smoldering Sword, I feel\nthat I must meet his expectations.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Bel_m01: <BLN>Mars.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dit_m01_001: I have been in this land a long time now. Perhaps I\nshould send Elfrida a gift.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dit_m01_002: Balor's head? No...she would likely send it right back.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dit_m01_003: What I do matters not. I am in for a lecture. There is\nno doubt about that.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Dit_m01: <BLN>I have been here a long time.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tal_m01_001: My bloodline has got to be the wildest mishmash\nof good-for-nothings out there, right?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tal_m01_002: If I had to work for any of my relatives, I'd quit so\nfast it'd make their heads spin.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tal_m01_003: Doubt they'd make decent employees either. End of\nthe day, I'm sure they'd ruin whatever they touch.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Tal_m01: <BLN>My bloodline is...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Orh_m01_001: I wonder if Aurora is safe. I heard she escaped from\nDagsion during the war.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Orh_m01_002: Aurora and her priests are also confronting Balor's\ngreat evil.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Orh_m01_003: She is so like you, bearing the hopes of the people\non her shoulders.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Orh_m01_004: Promised One, please... Could you make sure that\nshe is looked after in all this?
MID_LGA_3_M05_Orh_m01: <BLN>Promised One...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Seo_m01_001: The soldiers of Saramis have sharpened their skills\non the armies of the underworld.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Seo_m01_002: Those who survived the relentless battles were left all\nthe stronger for it.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Seo_m01_003: Warriors of Saramis do not fear death. They gird\nthemselves in their pride like armor.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Seo_m01_004: I pray that the soldiers and generals who have\nsurvived thus far see this war through to its end.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Seo_m01: <BLN>The soldiers of Saramis...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Led_m01_001: I look at the rubble, and I remember my hometown,\nKassite. The place I fled from with tears in my eyes...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Led_m01_002: But there's one difference. The risen dead scour\nthese towns and leave no one alive.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Led_m01_003: Heh, this war makes me so infuriated, I don't know\nwhat to do with all my anger.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Led_m01_004: I feel like I'm carrying the regrets of everyone\nwho died, and they're all spilling out.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Led_m01: <BLN>Looking at the rubble...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Anh_m01_001: Since leaving the village, I've found a liking for old\nanalog technology, like books.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Anh_m01_002: It's true, they don't store as much information as a\ndigital file can, and they cost resources to produce.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Anh_m01_003: But reading from paper makes it feel like the author\nis with you, sharing their feelings in real time.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Anh_m01_004: Whenever I find a book among the rubble, I do what\nI can to collect it and get it to safety.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Anh_m01: <BLN>Sharing their feelings...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tia_m01_001: When I'm playing games, sometimes I'll intentionally\nsacrifice a piece if doing so will ensure victory.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tia_m01_002: But that's a tactic I'd only ever practice on the board.\nNever in reality where real lives are at stake.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Tia_m01: <BLN>Only in board games...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Pet_m01_001: I've wanted to be a good-looking man ever since I\nwas a kid. But I'm not sure if I've become one.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Pet_m01_002: One thing I do know is it's a bad look to flee from\nbattle just because it's tough!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Pet_m01_003: That's what I keep telling myself at least. If nothing\nelse, it keeps me in the fight.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Pet_m01: <BLN>I want to be good-looking...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hur_m01_001: There are three things I think are important. Food,\nshelter, and a chance to bathe.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hur_m01_002: The Dagsion thermae were a symbol of everyday life.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hur_m01_003: After relaxing in the warmth for a bit, you start to\nfeel like you can fight again. It's no small thing.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Hur_m01: <BLN>Food, home, then...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Max_m01_001: Since I joined this war as a knight, I've thought a lot\nabout my time in Arago.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Max_m01_002: I don't mean my time with the Order of the Haze,\nbut when Bertrand taught me how to hold a blade...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Max_m01_003: and when his father, Geigart, told me the meaning\nof knighthood.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Max_m01_004: Those are the experiences that really made me who\nI am today.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Max_m01: <BLN>I ruminate on that.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gol_m01_001: The other day I ran into a kusarik outside the city.\nWas plannin' to catch it and cook it up.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gol_m01_002: But then the risen dead came shamblin' in. Before I\nknew it, the kusarik and me were on the same side!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gol_m01_003: Once we'd knocked out all of 'em, I gave the beastie\na long look...and then let him go.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gol_m01_004: Just a short truce between the living. But if I see\nit again, you know I'm havin' it for dinner! Bwahaha!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Gol_m01: <BLN>We had a truce.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gat_m01_001: In such an unprecedented war, I'm not certain my\nexperience as a general counts for much.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gat_m01_002: No warrior—no matter how seasoned—has seen the\nland of Dagda transformed into the underworld.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gat_m01_003: Still, we must stand before our anxious soldiers as\ntheir confident leaders.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Gat_m01: <BLN>It is unprecedented.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dan_m01_001: Most transcription houses and temples are\nin disarray, making it difficult to publish my works.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dan_m01_002: Meanwhile, the plays I've written the last few years\nexceeded what can be counted with all your fingers!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dan_m01_003: We must strive for victory, and restore the\napparatuses of publishing, for my audience's sake!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Dan_m01: <BLN>It is critical!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fab_m01_001: Unbelievable. Everywhere I turn, some priest begs\nme to lead them in prayer to the goddess.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fab_m01_002: I chose this skin as a convenient disguise—\nnothing more.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fab_m01_003: I never anticipated I would be asked to perform as\na holy man...
MID_LGA_3_M05_Fab_m01: <BLN>Unbelievable.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Esm_m01_001: When something bad happens, just look at the sea to\ncalm down. It's big, and it's always there for you.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Esm_m01_002: And on the other side of the sea is Sweetie's\nhome...Fódlan.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Esm_m01_003: I really want to go there someday. You should\ncome too!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Esm_m01: <BLN>Just look at the sea.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Urs_m01_001: Talimun's the one who taught me how to\ndefend myself.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Urs_m01_002: Though, nowadays, I primarily use my abilities to\nprotect others.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Urs_m01_003: How things change... To think I went from not\nbelieving in anything to being who I am now.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Urs_m01: <BLN>Things change.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sim_m01_001: Might sound crazy, but seeing so many dead all the\ntime almost makes me feel dead myself.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sim_m01_002: Did I already die? Am I trapped in the underworld?\nFeels like I'm going crazy, honestly...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sim_m01_003: It's looking at you that lets me know I'm alive.\nAs long as you're around, I know I'm OK.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Sim_m01: <BLN>C'mon, get a grip.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lou_m01_001: Apparently my father, General Senghor, sent letters\nto all my siblings. They said...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lou_m01_002: "We are not gods or beings with divine blood—we\nare family. And that is what will bring us victory."
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lou_m01_003: Father... I'm your daughter too, which is exactly why\nI won't lose. Just you watch!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Lou_m01: <BLN>Watch me!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fia_m01_001: A priest once asked me how I still have faith in a\nworld like ours... To be honest, I was a little stumped.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fia_m01_002: I don't know if my prayers truly reach any gods.\nBut, to me, it doesn't matter.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fia_m01_003: I pray because I want to help the world and its\npeople. That's it.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Fia_m01: <BLN>I had to ask myself why...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Die_m01_001: Given what's happening, it makes me sad to see\nanyone who seems broken and closed off.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Die_m01_002: I was like that long ago, suffering from despair,\nfeeling beyond rescue.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Die_m01: <BLN>It makes me sad...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lor_m01_001: It's depressing to see people I know among the\nrisen dead, even if it's someone I hate.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lor_m01_002: I can't imagine how that'd feel, to be forced to fight,\neven when you're dead. It's...so disturbing.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lor_m01_003: I've been thinking about this for a while, but I still\ncan't come to terms with it...
MID_LGA_3_M05_Lor_m01: <BLN>It's depressing...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Set_m01_001: I knew someone like you once—a figure who took to\nthe battlefield robed in white.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Set_m01_002: Her fighting style was so intense, I worried that it\nwould shatter who she was at heart.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Set_m01_003: But you're curiously calm during all of this. It must\ncome down to those you've gathered around you.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Set_m01_004: I hope you consider me someone who's helped to\nsome extent. Serving your cause is an honor.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Set_m01: <BLN>I knew someone like you.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nin_m01_001: I am pleased to share that spirits never change.\nYes, indeed, very pleased.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nin_m01_002: Those dears will never turn into the risen dead, as\nspirits aren't living beings whatsoever.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nin_m01_003: But, oh... Are my words very peculiar? I hoped they\nwould not be.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Nin_m01: <BLN>They never change...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Bon_m01_001: A proverb passed down among the children of\nDamascar goes "Life is a journey; death is a return."
MID_LGV_3_M05_Bon_m01_002: It means that our lives here are but a temporary\ndiversion before our souls return to a land of peace.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Bon_m01_003: By those lights, the risen dead are wayward souls,\nunable to return to their proper home. I pity them.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Bon_m01: <BLN>As the proverb says...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tob_m01_001: I'm getting low on hair oil. I'm gonna need a new\nbatch soon.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tob_m01_002: All the stores here have run out though. Supplies\nare running thin 'cause of the war.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tob_m01_003: Will what I've got last me until the war ends? Guess\nit depends on how hard we fight!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Tob_m01: <BLN>Hmm...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lil_m01_001: I hope my mother and father are still safe. I've been\ntoo busy to stop by home.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lil_m01_002: Gotta go see them first thing after this war is over,\nwhether I've got the money I need or not.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Lil_m01: <BLN>I hope they're both safe.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lys_m01_001: We must always be thinking of ways to rebuild this\ndevastated world.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lys_m01_002: The restoration will need leaders to oversee the\npeople's efforts and guide them properly.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Lys_m01_003: I see it as a noble's time to shine.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Lys_m01: <BLN>We must think ahead.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Buc_m01_001: One of my former trainees has joined your army.\nShe was effusive about her respect for you.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Buc_m01_002: She told me, "When I hear the savior's voice,\nmy sorrow dissipates. I feel emboldened."
MID_LGV_3_M05_Buc_m01_003: You have a gift for leadership that clearly made an\nimpact on her. I hope I can learn to emulate it.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Buc_m01: <BLN>I have much to learn from you.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sci_m01_001: It used to be mainly women flocking to me when I\nsang and played.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sci_m01_002: But since the war began, I have begun drawing in\nmen as well.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sci_m01_003: I know they seek comfort in my song, but they are\ncrowding out the beauties!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sci_m01_004: We must restore peace as soon as possible—for the\nsake of my love life.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Sci_m01: <BLN>We must restore peace.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Moo_m01_001: Promised One, are you tired? Want some coffee?\nI'll make it special!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Moo_m01_002: Well, I say "coffee." It's actually a substitute made\nfrom nuts and medicinal herbs.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Moo_m01_003: I did a lot of research and made something just as\ndelicious, but which also helps you sleep at night!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Moo_m01: <BLN>Cup of coffee?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mic_m01_001: I didn't have much to work with, but I baked the\nchildren some treats.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mic_m01_002: They turned out well. The kids liked 'em, anyway.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mic_m01_003: Even after the war ends, I'll keep at my mercenary\nwork. But being a baker would be nice too.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Mic_m01: <BLN>I baked some treats.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Oly_m01_001: Promised One, I hope you're getting your sleep.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Oly_m01_002: The extreme stress of a war erodes body and\nmind alike, so rest is paramount.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Oly_m01_003: If it might help, I can play you a song of the very\nhighest quality!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Oly_m01: <BLN>Are you rested?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Naz_m01_001: Sometimes, when I'm practicing at the training\ngrounds, soldiers want to talk to me.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Naz_m01_002: They ask if I'll teach them what I know. It's nice, but\nalso kind of awkward to be asked to teach.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Naz_m01_003: I wonder if Master Long ever felt this way when he\ntrained me and Anatolia?
MID_LGA_3_M05_Naz_m01: <BLN>It's nice, but awkward.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sar_m01_001: You're always on the go. I see you running all over\nfor so many people.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sar_m01_002: Are you taking care of yourself? Sleeping enough?\nPlease don't push yourself too hard.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sar_m01_003: Your body is much stronger than mine, but fatigue\nwill still build up if you aren't careful.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Sar_m01: <BLN>Don't push yourself too hard.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dai_m01_001: You know why you remind me of Anatolia? Because\neveryone is happy when you're around.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Dai_m01_002: No matter how bad things got in the village, she\ninspired everybody to give it their all.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Dai_m01: <BLN>You remind me of her.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hal_m01_001: Beating the risen dead feels impossible sometimes.\nIt takes everything I have just to survive.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hal_m01_002: Even so, I don't let that keep me from practicing my\ntricks! I gotta practice, or I won't be any good.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hal_m01_003: Fun is important! People need to be entertained!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Hal_m01: <BLN>Fun is important!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Guj_m01_001: The underworld gates are giving us a deep look into\nthe past! We're meeting the great people of history!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Guj_m01_002: This is the best way TO learn about history!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Guj_m01: <BLN>What an education!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Yan_m01_001: It appears that some souls I've saved have known\nme by the tattoo on my shoulder.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Yan_m01_002: My true name is unknown to them, so those people\nare calling me the "flower guy."
MID_LGV_3_M05_Yan_m01_003: That has a nice ring to it. We ought to have more\nflowers in our discussions about one another!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Yan_m01: <BLN>Not bad at all...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Iio_m01_001: Rocinan and I have known each other for a long\ntime, and he still looks after me today.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Iio_m01_002: It's not unlike soldiers being paired off, watching\neach other's backs.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Iio_m01_003: But Rocinan is even more than that to me. He's a\ntruly unique steed—and a close friend.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Iio_m01: <BLN>How to describe him...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Pep_m01_001: Some are submitting to despair, facing the darkness\nthat Balor has continued to spread.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Pep_m01_002: They fear that all living things will succumb to this\nkind of death. But we don't believe this.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Pep_m01_003: We can see the future ahead... Our own kingdom of\nBrigid—happy, smiling, and prospering!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Pep_m01_004: Do you find our optimism to be nonsense, given\nthe present, Promised One?
MID_LGA_3_M05_Pep_m01: <BLN>We can see it already!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Noc_m01_001: I love a good fight, even in times like this. Others\ndo too, you know...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Noc_m01_002: People I don't even know come right up to me and\nsay I'm being too excited about all of this.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Noc_m01_003: What look should I have on my face then? Should I\nmake myself look depressed?
MID_LGA_3_M05_Noc_m01: <BLN>What should I do?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sop_m01_001: I'm so hungry... Could that big ol' Bally send me\nsome risen dead made of food?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sop_m01_002: I mean, desperate times, right? So I've thought that\nseeds, in the dead, could grow like in gardens...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Sop_m01_003: And so it's not all that silly to hope for the risen dead\nto bring us food, right? Well...maybe it is...
MID_LGA_3_M05_Sop_m01: <BLN>I'm so hungry...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cat_m01_001: Yet again, I saved some people in the most brilliant\nfashion. I'm becoming quite the celebrated hero!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cat_m01_002: That's just to be expected, of course. Admiration\nfollows me around!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Cat_m01: <BLN>I deliver results!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ned_m01_001: Saramis has been thought of as a strange kingdom\nthat worshipped a terrible "god of death."
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ned_m01_002: But after all the warring since Dagda's return,\nother countries are seeing Saramis in a new light.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ned_m01_003: I know that I left my country long ago, but the\nthought of this makes me a bit happy.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Ned_m01: <BLN>It makes me a bit happy.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Zac_m01_001: Eh, the good ol' days, when I could pickpocket\njust anyone walking by...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Zac_m01_002: Is it too much to ask to go back to folks being\neasy prey?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Zac_m01_003: Why the hell do I have to fight tooth and nail\nagainst the risen dead all the time?!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Zac_m01: <BLN>Why? Whyyy?!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Maj_m01_001: Kind of late to be figurin' this out...but Balor sure has\na crazy amount of power for a corpse.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Maj_m01_002: Huh, but does that mean the corpse of the great\nMajide will cause something huge like all this?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Maj_m01_003: I should make sure my tomb's all good 'n sealed up.\nI'd hate for someone to mess with me!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Maj_m01: <BLN>Does that mean...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ven_m01_001: Youths these days! No patience! They don't bother\nto listen to the end of my stories!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ven_m01_002: I see how they look at me! And the things they say!\n"I've heard that one before..." How DARE they!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ven_m01_003: For the record, I repeat my stories on purpose!\nThey should shut up and enjoy it!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Ven_m01: <BLN>Making a fool out of me?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ini_m01_001: When I feel anxious, I like to get in some training\nwith my bow.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ini_m01_002: Then I can focus, putting distractions aside, and I\ncome back to myself more and more.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Ini_m01: <BLN>When I feel anxious...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Jas_m01_001: I wonder if he'll turn up...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Jas_m01_002: Even if he's the risen dead, controlled by Balor, I'd\nstill like to see him again.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Jas_m01_003: I'd be so hurt if he attacked me though. Boy, that's a\nwhole lot of messy thoughts, huh?
MID_LGA_3_M05_Jas_m01: <BLN>I wonder...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ale_m01_001: With the world as it is, I don't have many chances to\ntake a leisurely flight through the sky.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ale_m01_002: I used to do that often if I had free time. Just soar\nthrough the sky... Now patrols are my life.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ale_m01_003: Still, that does protect a lot of people, so I'm glad to\npatrol from the sky with everything I've got.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Ale_m01: <BLN>No leisurely flights...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cen_m01_001: I'm thinking about how people's faith is a source\nof hope.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cen_m01_002: However, Aurora, a deity, aspired to live life as\na simple mortal.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cen_m01_003: Eventually, god or no, they will all pass. I cannot\neven imagine the world with no gods.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Cen_m01: <BLN>A world with no gods...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kir_m01_001: There's been a rascal who's been followin' me around\nfor years. Wants to be a pirate. But he's too decent.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kir_m01_002: He told me he gave food to a hungry kid—that he\nfelt bad and had no choice.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kir_m01_003: But I promised him I'd take him into my crew. I'm\ngonna have the world's nicest bunch o' pirates, huh?
MID_LGA_3_M05_Kir_m01: <BLN>He's too decent...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nuz_m01_001: The underworld invading our world gave me\nsomething to consider.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nuz_m01_002: What is the nature of the soul? And from where does\nit draw its power?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nuz_m01_003: But these philosophical questions don't win battles.\nYet another way in which I am weak, I fear.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Nuz_m01: <BLN>What is the nature of the soul?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fot_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fot_m01_001: 'Tis good, I suppose, that the children of Dagsion\nhave grown less skittish around me.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fot_m01_002: But can you explain to me why they never tire of\noffering me sweets?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fot_m01_003: They're hardly more than boiled sugar, but even\nlow-quality confections are hard to come by now.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fot_m01_004: If the temple storehouses contain any sweets, I say\nwe disburse them among the children!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Fot_m01_005: After setting aside my share, naturally.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Fot_m01: <BLN>See that it's done!
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kou_m01_001: Enough people have flocked to Dagsion that it's\nalmost as lively as it used to be.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kou_m01_002: Though the citizens from those days can\nnever return...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kou_m01_003: How can I possibly make amends to them?
MID_LGA_3_M05_Kou_m01: <BLN>What can I do?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tro_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tro_m01_001: I don't know how you think of me, but I consider\nmyself a big sister to you.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tro_m01_002: <NCA>"Is that so?"
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tro_m01_003: <NCB>"I think of you as a trusted ally."
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tro_m01_004: <ACA>Don't get me wrong—Zenon told me who you are.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tro_m01_005: <ACA>But since we're both Mediators now, I'm the one\nwith more experience at it.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tro_m01_006: <ACB>As you should. I'm here to smooth the way for the\nrest of you.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tro_m01_007: <ACB>After all, it's natural for the old to go first.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tro_m01_008: You're off to a great start, but when the time comes,\nremember your big sister's advice.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Tro_m01: <BLN>I've been where you are.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Asw_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Asw_m01_001: We're all doing our utmost to reclaim this world.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Asw_m01_002: Seeing the people around me expend such effort...\nIt gives me courage.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Asw_m01_003: I suppose I'll have to redouble my efforts. Ahaha.\nCan't let them show me up!
MID_LGA_3_M05_Asw_m01: <BLN>Everyone's working so hard.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tah_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tah_m01_001: You might not know it from looking at me, but I'm a\ndecent warrior.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tah_m01_002: I also picked up the Python Technique, a killing\nstyle from central Nysiades.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Tah_m01_003: Happy to teach it to you too, Promised One.\nIf you'd like.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Tah_m01: <BLN>It might be a surprise...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kra_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kra_m01_001: Our nation is officially known as the Mosa\nHoly State.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kra_m01_002: Our king can trace his bloodline directly to our god,\nwho created the world in ancient times.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kra_m01_003: You may have noticed our faith is pretty different\nfrom what's practiced here.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Kra_m01_004: We're somewhat skeptical to see gods taking an\nactive hand in ruling your nation.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Kra_m01: <BLN>About the Mosa...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nat_m01_001: I keep coming back to something my friend tells me.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Nat_m01_002: He says that while I'm usually stuffy and rational,\nwhen the fight starts, I charge in like a fool.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Nat_m01: <BLN>He tells me all the time.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hri_m01_001: What will this continent look like after the war?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hri_m01_002: I doubt, after Dagda the Great's atrocities, it will\nagain be an empire founded on faith in the gods.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hri_m01_003: You may not be open to this...but I suspect few\nwould object to your becoming the new leader.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Hri_m01_004: If that happened, I'd lend you my spear, certainly.\nBut I'll leave it there.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Hri_m01: <BLN>What will the future look like?
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ann_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ann_m01_001: My bloodmark was the reason Lord Solel kept me\nby his side.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ann_m01_002: But in the end, I never had a chance to use it. I'm not\nsure what he had in mind there.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Ann_m01_003: Which one do I have? Well, I don't know much about\nit, but I think it's called the Diadem of the Fanatic.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Ann_m01: <BLN>My bloodmark...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mys_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mys_m01_001: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mys_m01_002: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mys_m01_003: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mys_m01_004: 
MID_LGA_3_M05_Mys_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cle_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cle_m01_001: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cle_m01_002: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cle_m01_003: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cle_m01_004: 
MID_LGA_3_M05_Cle_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gra_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gra_m01_001: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gra_m01_002: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Gra_m01_003: 
MID_LGA_3_M05_Gra_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M05_Jun_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Jun_m01_001: I always thought Fortuna was an odd one.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Jun_m01_002: Don't let her youthful appearance fool you. She has\na certain detachment that sets her apart from us.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Jun_m01_003: I often found it strange that Dagda the Great took\nsuch pains to avoid her.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Jun_m01: <BLN>Fortuna's looks are deceiving.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mar_m01_001: You're a mystery, Promised One. You're at once\nimposing and good at drawing people in.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mar_m01_002: Your aura reminds me of someone.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Mar_m01_003: Though I suppose it could just be a quality of\nMediators that you're all endowed with.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Mar_m01: <BLN>It's a mystery.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Smi_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Smi_m01_001: If I really consider it, I've always been fond of my\nhalf brother Credna.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Smi_m01_002: He too...is unpredictable. You never know what\nhe'll do next.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Smi_m01_003: And then there's you... Such an enigmatic air!\nI like that quality.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Smi_m01: <BLN>I like that...
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cla_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cla_m01_001: I was surprised to see you talking to Fortuna. She\nseems to trust you.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cla_m01_002: I've never seen her express herself to anyone in\nthat way before.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Cla_m01_003: This is a rare chance for me to speak to her. It's been\na good while since I last did.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Cla_m01: <BLN>I was surprised.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Car_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Car_m01_001: I see more brightness in the faces of the city's people.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Car_m01_002: They believe in you. Believe you will strike down\nBalor and bring light to this dark world.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Car_m01: <BLN>They believe in you.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Aur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_Aur_m01_001: The city recovered so quickly.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Aur_m01_002: Humans are such a resilient lot.
MID_LGV_3_M05_Aur_m01_003: I'm certain it's in no small part thanks to the hope\nyou inspire in them, Promised One.
MID_LGA_3_M05_Aur_m01: <BLN>So quickly...
MID_LGV_3_M05_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B01_m01_001: When I have daily necessities in stock, I get a lot of\noffers to buy them in bulk, even at double the price.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B01_m01_002: I generally turn them down. It's important that they\nget to as many people as possible.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B01_m01_003: "Double the price" is a tempting offer though. I need\nto weigh the situation carefully.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B01_m01: <BLN>A merchant walks a fine line...
MID_LGV_3_M05_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B02_m01_001: The world's a mess, and as a noncombatant, I have\nno power to do anything about it.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B02_m01_002: All I've come up with is to set about crafting things\nlike prosthetic limbs.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B02_m01_003: Hopefully this way, I can improve the lives of the\nones who've survived the horrors. That counts...right?
MID_LGA_3_M05_B02_m01: <BLN>Am I really doing my part?
MID_LGV_3_M05_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B03_m01_001: I'm trying to think up a new board game. I'm gonna\ntake one I already have and tinker with it a little.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B03_m01_002: One of the pieces is gonna be based on you,\nPromised One! It'll be the strongest!
MID_LGA_3_M05_B03_m01: <BLN>I'm thinking up a new game!
MID_LGV_3_M05_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B04_m01_001: Some of the kids who couldn't stop crying over the\nrisen dead have started to remember how to smile.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B04_m01_002: I think it's sinking in with them that they're safe\nhere. That's thanks to you, Promised One.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B04_m01: <BLN>Thank you.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B05_m01_001: When I first made it here, I was tired and listless.\nBut lately, I've been helping out in the fields.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B05_m01_002: Staying busy helps when I remember my daughter\nwho passed away. It's slowly getting easier.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B05_m01: <BLN>I'm helping out in the fields.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B06_m01_001: A great many people have come here to pray today.\nAll of them are wishing for your safety.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B06_m01_002: I find it personally moving that the people continue\nto pray. Even this war-torn world hasn't killed hope.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B06_m01: <BLN>Many have come here to pray.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B07_m01_001: I only survived in battle long enough to make it home\nbecause of Mars's protection.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B07_m01_002: If you start to think you're too good to die, that's\nwhen it's over for you.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B07_m01: <BLN>Only the Bringer of War saved me.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B08_m01_001: A world where the dead come back to kill you is\nterrifying, but I have to stay brave for my kids.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B08_m01_002: I come to the temple to let my feelings out in prayer.\nOnce I'm back home, I have to be the strong father.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B08_m01: <BLN>I can be honest here.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B09_m01_001: A priest told me Lord Solel was the one who made\nthe map of Dagda.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B09_m01_002: But the war must have changed stuff...so someone\nshould make a new one! Maybe me?
MID_LGA_3_M05_B09_m01: <BLN>Do we need a new map?
MID_LGV_3_M05_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B10_m01_001: This is going to sound strange, but my marriage has\nactually improved since this war started.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B10_m01_002: We didn't spend much time together in our mansion.\nSometimes we went days without talking.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B10_m01_003: But ever since we arrived, we've relied on each other\nmore. Poverty's the best thing that's happened to me.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B10_m01: <BLN>I'm glad we lost everything.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B11_m01_001: After I got here, I borrowed abandoned household\ngoods to scrape by.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B11_m01_002: The original owners were dead, and I'm alive, so I\nscavenged what I needed and didn't think twice.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B11_m01_003: But now that my life is starting to be stable again,\nI'm putting them back where I found them.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B11_m01: <BLN>I'm putting it all back.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B12_m01_001: It's been three years since my husband passed...\nI thought about joining him in death, but I couldn't.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B12_m01_002: And I'm glad for that now. If I hadn't lived, I couldn't\nhave helped out with the rebuilding effort.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B12_m01: <BLN>I made the right decision.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B13_m01_001: Only lately have I been able to think things like\n"What should I do tomorrow?"
MID_LGV_3_M05_B13_m01_002: Before, every part of me was focused on survival.\nI didn't have space for anything else.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B13_m01: <BLN>Things are changing, day by day.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B14_m01_001: I caught a fat fish as big as my arm, and we all ate it\ntogether. Although I only had a couple bites.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B14_m01_002: Still, I enjoyed it more than if I'd kept it all for\nmyself. I think most folks feel that way now.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B14_m01: <BLN>There's enough for everyone!
MID_LGV_3_M05_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B15_m01_001: My missing grandpa is back! I guess he'd been\nhiding in a cave.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B15_m01_002: Our whole family had given up hope. I feel sorta\nguilty about that now.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B15_m01: <BLN>I feel sorta guilty.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B16_m01_001: Everyone has hope in their hearts after all you've\ndone for us, Promised One. It's beautiful to see.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B16_m01_002: But not everyone has found safety yet. I hope you'll\nkeep going until then...
MID_LGA_3_M05_B16_m01: <BLN>There's hope for us yet!
MID_LGV_3_M05_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B17_m01_001: I heard that Lord Solel's mistress used to live in the\nCrystal Palace.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B17_m01_002: Apparently she was a beautiful woman, but I guess\nDagda the Great put her to death like everyone else.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B17_m01: <BLN>The Crystal Palace...
MID_LGV_3_M05_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B18_m01_001: Thanks to so many people finding refuge here, we\nhave artisans in a wide range of disciplines.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B18_m01_002: We plan to work together to make Dagsion an even\nmore beautiful city than it was.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B18_m01_003: The project will take years, but we're all excited to\nsee it through.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B18_m01: <BLN>We'll get it done.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M05_B19_m01_001: I used to work as a servant around here. Our master\nwas a disgusting man.
MID_LGV_3_M05_B19_m01_002: He hounded me so much that I had nightmares about\nhim even after I quit. Though...I guess he's dead now.
MID_LGA_3_M05_B19_m01: <BLN>I used to work as a servant.